  "implementation": "The probe splits the original prompt into two 456-position graphs. Each streamed projection groups routed rows by 32 consecutive experts, reads the original GGUF bytes into a single charged Metal tile and scatters only real output rows. Unused rows in a 256-row projection work buffer have valid indices and are discarded; no token is appended to the prompt. Synchronization precedes tile reuse. After prefill, it releases the enlarged scheduler and reserves the usual decode graph; recurrent state, target feature rows and KV outlive this scheduler. Counters named prefill_windows refer to the legacy three-buffer bank only. The new path is opt-in and qualified here on this fixture alone.",
